Season player stats Historical Held and queryable, but not currently being ingested. Last ingested 2026-06-03. Endpoint /v1/nba/players/:id/splits Last updated 2026-06-03 Fields ( 46 ) Ast %, Ast Ratio, Ast to, Defensive Rating, Dreb %, E Defensive Rating, E Net Rating, E Offensive Rating, E Pace, E Tov %, E Usg %, Efg %, Games Played, Losses, Minutes, Net Rating, Offensive Rating, Oreb %, Pace, Pace Per40, Pie, Poss, Rebounds %, Tm Tov %, Ts %, Usg %, W %, Wins, Ast, Blk, Dreb, Fg3 %, Fg3a, Fg3m, FG %, Fga, Fgm, Ft %, Fta, Ftm, Oreb, Pf, Points, Rebounds, Stl, Turnover Team stats (per game) Post-game Written after the game ends — not a live in-game feed. Last ingested 2026-09-16. Endpoint /v1/matches/:id/statistics Last updated 2026-09-16 Fields ( 26 ) Assists, Blocks, Defensive Rebounds, Fast Break Points, Field Goal %, Field Goals Made/Attempted, Flagrant Fouls, Personal Fouls, Free Throw %, Free Throws Made/Attempted, Largest Lead, Lead Changes, Time Leading %, Offensive Rebounds, Points in the Paint, Score, Steals, Team Turnovers, Technical Fouls, Three-Point %, Three Point Field Goals Made/Attem, Total Rebounds, Total Technical Fouls, Total Turnovers, Turnover Points, Turnovers Not included Not shown here — player_per_game_box (new granularity, not yet mapped for display). Not shown here — player_season_general: 176 raw upstream season keys with no route serving them. Not shown here — play_by_play: play-by-play events, not a stat line — mostly identifiers once classified. Not shown here — lineups: lineup composition, not a measured stat. Not shown here — props: betting lines and prices, not stats — they belong on the odds surface. player_season is not currently ingesting (last 2026-06-02). player_season_advanced is not currently ingesting (last 2026-06-03). Missing a stat? We build what people actually ask for. If a field you need is not on this page, tell us — requests are how we decide what to add next. Which basketball stat do you need? Name the field or the endpoint shape. Specifics help more than categories. Email (optional — only if you want a reply) Send request Goes straight to the team as a product signal. No newsletter, no account, nothing else done with your address. What you can build Player props tracker Surface prop hit rates over the last N games and find the edge before tip-off. Live score widget Embed real-time NBA scores and quarter-by-quarter linescores on any site. Fantasy / DFS optimizer Season averages, matchup stats, and injury status in one feed. Matchup preview page The full matchup — season stats, last-5, rest days, roster, H2H — in one call. Historical analytics 13.6M plays and 70,611 games back to 1946 for backtesting and ML training sets. Betting research tool Odds, against-the-spread records, and player-prop ladders in one place. See which endpoints are free : Free Sports API: 114 Free Endpoints . Walk through it end to end: How to build a fantasy basketball app . Endpoints On the gateway at api.bigballsdata.com . Authenticate with the bearer token from /dashboard/keys . Click any endpoint to see every field it returns. 9 endpoint s · 135 documented fields. Click any row to see every field it returns. GET NBA Matchup · intelligence endpoint Free 55 fields ▾ GET NBA Player Splits · home / away / form splits Free 12 fields ▾ GET Player Injury · current injury status Free 12 fields ▾ GET League Injuries · the whole NBA report Free 10 fields ▾ GET NBA Lineups · starters + bench per side Free 5 fields ▾ GET NBA Player Game Log · flat per-game box lines Free 19 fields ▾ GET NBA Player Career Averages · season-by-season averages Free 12 fields ▾ GET NBA Team Playoff Record · per-season playoff wins Free 5 fields ▾ GET NBA Game Lineups · Starters and bench Free 5 fields ▾ Start on the free tier 100 requests per minute and 250 per day, free — the highest per-minute burst of any free sports API we checked. Burst is what matters when something asks several questions in a row and waits on each answer. Every sport and league we cover — the paid tiers add history depth and premium fields, not more leagues. Calls are counted one for one — no credit weighting, no markets-times-regions arithmetic. Link GitHub and the daily cap goes to 500 . No credit card. Get a key → Or ask your AI tool directly Connect your account to Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, Perplexity or any other MCP-compatible tool and ask for basketball data in conversation — scores, standings, player stats and Elo ratings, with no API key to paste and no code to write. Your plan and limits carry over exactly as they do here. Connect your AI tool → Integrate in a few lines Node.js, @bigballsdata/sdk typescript import { BigBallSportsClient } from &#x27;@bigballsdata/sdk&#x27;; const client = new BigBallSportsClient(process.env.BBS_API_KEY!); // The SDK has no `nba` namespace — this surface is REST-only today. const headers = { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.BBS_API_KEY}` }; const API = &#x27;https://api.bigballsdata.com&#x27;; const games = await fetch(`${API}/v1/matches?league=nba&limit=50`, { headers }).then((r) => r.json()); // Source-native archive games deliberately have no v1 match bridge. Pick a // bridged row only because the legacy matchup resource requires match_id. const bridged = games.data.find((game: { match_id: string | null }) => game.match_id); if (!bridged) throw new Error(&#x27;No bridged NBA game in this page; request the next offset.&#x27;); const matchup = await fetch(`${API}/v1/nba/games/${bridged.match_id}/matchup`, { headers }) .then((r) => r.json()); for (const p of matchup.data.home_team.players) { console.log(p.name, p.season_averages?.pts?.toFixed(1) ?? &#x27;-&#x27;, &#x27;ppg&#x27;); } Free covers a real app. Scale when you need to. 250 req/day free (500 with GitHub). Production starts at $49/mo. Live WebSocket push on Pro+. See all plans → Frequently asked Is there a free NBA API? Yes. The API covers scores, box scores, standings, player profiles, and injury reports. There is a free tier; pricing lists what each plan covers. Two NBA data types are paid: odds start at Edge ($149/mo), and play-by-play — including shot coordinates — is Pro. Full play-by-play logs are Pro for basketball, hockey and football, not just the NBA. Scoring plays stay free on every sport. Free keys get 250 req/day (500 with GitHub). No credit card. Does the NBA API include player props? Yes. /v1/nba/players/:player_id/props returns the latest prop line we hold plus a rolling hit rate over the last N games, computed from box scores. Every response carries a `freshness` block derived from the line’s own timestamp (`data_as_of`, age in days, and a status of live/recent/stale). Read freshness.status rather than assuming a returned line is a current price: when nothing is on the board the newest line we hold can be days or weeks old, and the block says so in the response. Most competitors do not offer prop hit rates at all. How far back does NBA historical data go? To the 1946–47 season. The unified archive holds 70,611 archive-backed games plus canonical match-only coverage, queryable through /v1/matches?league=nba. The separate play-by-play resource holds 13.6M events through 2023 at /v1/nba/games/:game_id/plays. Useful for backtesting and ML training sets. Can I get live NBA scores and play-by-play? Yes. The REST scores endpoint refreshes on a 15-second cache during live games (~200ms typical round trip). WebSocket push for score updates is on the Pro plan. Is there an NBA play-by-play API? Yes. /v1/nba/games/:game_id/plays returns event-level play-by-play, 13.6M plays across the 1946-2023 archive, with period, game clock, the players involved, running score, and a scoring-play flag on every event. Filterable by period and player. Play-by-play is a Pro-plan endpoint — on every sport, not just the NBA — and a Free, Solo, Trio or Edge key gets a 403 with an upgrade hint. Does the NBA API have betting odds? Yes, in two forms. The archive: archived closing-line snapshots, plus a T-24h snapshot, for finished NBA games on /v1/odds/historical — enough depth to backtest against real closing lines, with meta.snapshot_types_present naming what each response contains and /v1/coverage reporting the covered-game count under data_types.odds_historical. Live pricing: /v1/matches/:id/odds returns pre-match and in-play odds (moneyline, spread, totals) across 16+ sportsbooks while games are on the board, and nothing when none are — /v1/coverage reports freshness.next_event so you can tell which case you are in. Odds require the Edge plan ($149/mo) or higher; scores, standings, lineups, stats, and scoring events stay on the free tier. Can I get NBA shot coordinates? Yes. /v1/players/:id/shots returns per-shot court coordinates (coordinate_x, coordinate_y) with shot type, distance, and make/miss for the 2025-26 season. See the dedicated NBA Shot Chart API page (/nba-shot-chart-api) for the full response shape. Related APIs Other APIs you can build with: Basketball API — Every League, One Schema WNBA API NCAA Basketball API How we compare vs API-Sports vs The Odds API vs SportsData.io Also on this sport NBA Player Props API NBA Shot Chart API Stats reference NBA Player Stats API NBA Player Props API Odds & two-source verification Get an API key in 30 seconds Get API key, free Read the quickstart The sports data API built for ballers. Add to Google preferred sources Sports & Leagues Soccer Football Premier League La Liga Serie A Bundesliga Ligue 1 Champions League MLS World Cup 2026 Africa Cup of Nations CONCACAF Gold Cup Copa América Euro Championship UEFA Nations League Basketball NBA NCAA Basketball WNBA American Football NFL NCAAF (FBS & FCS) Baseball MLB Ice Hockey NHL Cricket MMA UFC Boxing Formula 1 Product Docs API Reference Pricing Coverage API Status Sports coverage League codes What&#x27;s new Blog About Datasets Injuries Live NBA Props Live NHL Props Live NBA Shot Chart MLB Odds MLB Pitch Data Free Sports API Tools Odds Calculator Parla